{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.modular_cannot_bridge'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.modular_cannot_bridge'","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.lean#L144-L151","doc":"The same statement from the substrate side: a nonzero purely-imaginary `b²`\nhas a purely-imaginary modular partner, never a real one.  So the substrate\ncannot reach the fibre regime either — the exclusion is symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.modular_cannot_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.modular_cannot_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.lean#L134-L142","doc":"**Attack B's mechanism is excluded.**  For a nonzero `b²` in the fibre\nlocus, the modular partner `1/b²` is *still* in the fibre locus and is NOT in\nthe substrate locus.  Modular inversion therefore cannot carry the `|q| = 1`\nelliptic regime to the real-`q` substrate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.loci_inter_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.loci_inter_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.lean#L126-L132","doc":"The two loci meet only at `0`.  `FaddeevPhi.hb` asserts `0 < Re b`, hence\n`b ≠ 0` and `b² ≠ 0`, so no admissible `b` sits on both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.substrate_inv_im_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.substrate_inv_im_neg","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.lean#L113-L122","doc":"On the substrate locus inversion FLIPS the sign of `Im b²`.  So it carries\nthe `Im b² > 0` branch — the one `PhiBProd` supports — to its own reflection,\nand that is the only motion it has there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.substrate_inv_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.substrate_inv_mem","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.lean#L107-L111","doc":"Inversion fixes the imaginary axis: the substrate locus maps into itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.fibre_inv_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.fibre_inv_mem","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.lean#L101-L105","doc":"Inversion fixes the real axis: the fibre locus maps into itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.InSubstrateLocus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.InSubstrateLocus","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.lean#L93-L97","doc":"The substrate regime on its principal branch: `q` real positive with\n`Re b² = 0`, i.e. `b²` purely imaginary.  (`q = exp(iπb²)` is real positive iff\n`Re b² ∈ 2ℤ`; the principal branch is the `0` cell, which is the one the\n`arg b = π/4` substrate branch lands in.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.InFibreLocus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.InFibreLocus","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleLocusSeparation.lean#L89-L91","doc":"The fibre / elliptic regime: `|q| = 1`, equivalently `b²` real.  Since\n`q = exp(iπb²)` has `|q| = exp(-π Im b²)`, this is exactly `Im b² = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}